Negative control for useCompositionPort.spec.ts (and, downstream, reflect.int.spec.ts).

Fabricates a table channel the caller never wired, so every module reads as
table-owning and `port.table` stops being the caller's own object.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Proven RED 2026-08-08 (`pnpm --filter @upmind-automation/labs-nuxt test`):
  x hands the caller's own channel through on port.table
      -> expected { read, emit } to be { read, emit } // Object.is equality
  x leaves port.table undefined for a module whose caller supplies no channel
      -> expected { read, emit } to be undefined
  x classifies a schema+model cell as form-flow   -> expected 'list' to be 'form-flow'
  x classifies a model-only cell as detail        -> expected 'list' to be 'detail'
  x classifies a bare-actions cell as action-panel -> expected 'list' to be 'action-panel'
  5 failed | 14 passed

